                <pb facs="0157" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Steering Committee/482: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-06-28T14:00:00+01:00">June 28, 1935—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 28—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>294. From Hugh Wilson. Henderson has confirmed to me approximately what I
                    reported recently from Geneva after conversation with Aghnides. He contemplates
                    calling a Bureau meeting for September 16th probably followed by a General
                    Commission meeting 10 days later.</p>
                <p>Henderson explained that the negotiations appeared to be taking a turn which for
                    good or evil is not in accordance with Conference procedure. He can no longer
                    assume the responsibility of allowing the Conference to lapse through inanition.
                    He feels he must share that responsibility with the Bureau. Unless at the Bureau
                    meeting there are indications of a speedy resumption of work Henderson will urge
                    the Bureau to adopt a resolution to lay before the General Commission the
                    question of the future of the Conference.</p>
                <p>Am writing Mr. Davis direct.</p>
                <p>Cipher text to Geneva. [Wilson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
